Chapter: SerialByteFlood
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 A byte written to UART data port 1016 (0x3F8) reaches codex-vm's capture
 through output_buf_write, one byte per exit (tools/codex-vm.c). Every
 print on codex-vm goes by the bulk blit instead, so nothing but a direct
 UART write fills that path. One print, then 300 bytes of 'x' to the UART;
 under CODEX_VM_FAIL_GROW_AT the byte path fills and drops the rest while
 the blit path drops nothing.

Section: Entry

  flood : Integer -> [Device.Port] Integer
  flood (i) = act
   w <- port-out-byte 1016 120
   if i <= 1 then w else flood (i - 1)
  end

  opening : [Console, Device.Port] Integer = act
   print-line-uni "flood"
   r <- flood 300
   r
  end
